			"notes": "# Minecraft Version(s): 26.3\n## Changes:\n- Added Moonweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while under the open night sky in the Overworld\n- Added Sunweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while under the open daytime sky in the Overworld\n- Added Rainweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while rain falls on you\n- Added Emberweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while in the Nether\n- Added Voidweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while in the End\n- Added Tideweave (Treasure, I-III): slowly repairs the enchanted item while your head is underwater\n- All weaves are incompatible with each other, Mending, Handyman and Sacrifice\n- Added Harpoon (Fishing Rods, I-III): reeled-in mobs get yanked towards you\n- Added Impale Rush (Spears, I-III): charged spear hits pin the target in place (incompatible with Lunge)\n- Added Updraft (Elytras, Treasure, I-III): gliding over lava, magma or fire lifts you up\n- Added Curse of Corrosion (Any Damageable): slowly drains durability in rain or underwater (incompatible with all repair enchantments)\n- Added Meteor (Maces, Treasure): smash attacks after falling 8 blocks set the area on fire (incompatible with Boltbringer)\n- Added Jousting (Spears, I-III): deals extra damage while riding a mount\n- Added Dismount (Spears): charged spear hits knock riders off their mounts\n- Added Yoink (Fishing Rods, I-III): reeling in a hooked mob steals its held item\n- Added Scholar of Fishing (Fishing Rods, I-III): increases the experience you get from fishing\n\n## Fixes:\n- Daytime detection predicate for Day Protection"
		},
